# Jak II, 0.1.8 (LIST-0.1.8 item 6, Steer by grabbing the wheel). Run with JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=ctysluma-start
# JAKVR_TEST_WARP=bikea JAKVR_TEST_RIDE=1 QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000 JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1: in Haven City Jak put and kept 2 m
# from the nearest city bike (frame 10000), which the test aid then puts him on as Triangle does. Riding (A: the throttle): both grips squeezed
# with the hands where they rest ahead (the wheel held: "[vr-pad] the wheel held by ..."), the hands turned as a wheel
# to the right (the right down, the left up), back, then as handlebars to the left (the right pushed ahead, the left
# pulled back), let go (the wheel back to the middle), the left hand alone turned down (the left side down: left),
# then a quick squeeze of the right grip on the wheel (R2: the bike's height), its squeeze again held (R2 held), and a
# grip squeezed with the hand low at the side (not the wheel's place: R2 at once). Then both hands on it again: the
# right stick's click ("... the right stick's click with that hand on the wheel: R2"), the left's, the wheel tilted
# back as a car's (the right down and back, the left up and ahead: steering right, as much as either alone would
# give), turned far past full lock, and back a little (the steering falls at once: the lock). Expect "[vr-pad] the
# wheel: turned ... steering ..." lines (the bike: handlebars, "the wheel held by ... handlebars or a bar") and the
# bike turning in the pictures.
